{
 "name": "calibration",
 "description": "Calibration: every compute primitive at fixed shapes, timed by the executor's node spans. Each node is named by its primitive and shape, so the protocol's node timings read as the table: forward-n{N}-b{B} (logits/read over B records of exactly N tokens, one record per row), decode-t{T}-n{n} (text/generate from a chat prompt that asks for a long story, T new tokens, n samples, seeded), capture-k{K}-n{N} (activations/capture-tokens at K layers over N positions, stored as tensor shards, so it also times io), lora-s20 (a 20-step adapter/train), and numeric-* (direction/classify and geometry/compare over a pooled capture of 128 labelled records at 8 layers). warmup-n1 runs first and absorbs model load. Inputs are fixed bench objects under benjismith/calibration; N is exact in the Gemma 4 tokenizer. Run it on your own machine with only the model bound; results union by node id.",
 "params": [
  {
   "name": "model",
   "type": "model",
